        {
          "type": "audio",
          "text_en": "Hi, I'm Mazen. I'm from Tarim and I'm in the third grade. On school days, I get up at five o'clock. I pray and then I have breakfast with my family. We have bread, beans and tea. I walk to school with my cousin. Lessons start at seven thirty. We finish at one o'clock and I have lunch at home at two. In the afternoon, I do my homework and I help my father in his shop. In the evening, I read or I talk to my friends. I go to bed at ten o'clock. I don't stay up late."
        },
