          "type": "reading",
          "text_en": "The Al-Kaff family live in a village near Tarim. Their day starts early. They get up at half past four. The father and the sons go to the mosque for the dawn prayer. Then they have breakfast together. The children walk to school. It is two kilometres from their house. In the afternoon, the girls help their mother, and the boys help their father on the date farm. They don't have a TV, but they have a radio. In the evening, they listen to the news and talk. They go to bed early, at nine o'clock, because they get up very early.",
